        <li>Nike delivered strong long-term compounding (+1,282.35%) despite deep cyclical drawdowns.</li>
        <li>The all-time low was $2.47 on 2000-02-25; the all-time high was $166.25 on 2021-11-05.</li>
        <li>Risk was materially path-dependent: post-2021 valuation compression produced the period's deepest peak-to-trough decline.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>Long-Term Price Trend Analysis</h2>
      <div id="priceChart" class="chart"></div>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Phase 1 (2000–2009):</strong> volatile accumulation period across dot-com unwind and GFC years, ending with gradual recovery structure.</li>
        <li><strong>Phase 2 (2010–2021):</strong> sustained secular uptrend with persistent higher highs, culminating at $166.25 on 2021-11-05.</li>
        <li><strong>Phase 3 (2021–2026):</strong> de-rating regime, including the dataset's maximum drawdown to $52.31 on 2025-04-08 before partial stabilization.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note">Interpretation focus: NKE behaved like a long-duration compounder over full horizon, but with equity-like cyclicality and major valuation resets.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <h2>Volatility and Risk Assessment</h2>
      <div class="two-col">
        <div><div id="rangeChart" class="chart"></div></div>
        <div><div id="volChart" class="chart"></div></div>
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li>Peak 20-day annualized volatility reached 107.98% on 2020-04-06, marking the most acute short-horizon risk regime.</li>
        <li>Full-period annualized volatility is 31.19%, indicating moderate-to-high single-name equity risk over long horizons.</li>
        <li>Maximum drawdown of -68.53% (2021-11-05 to 2025-04-08) demonstrates severe downside potential even after long outperformance.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

